new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b83208
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/source/argument_files.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+.. _Argument Files:
+
+==============
+Argument Files
+==============
+Deeply nested :doc:`user classes <user_classes>` can require long, repetitive command lines.
+Instead of typing them out, they can be stored in an **argument file** and referenced with a single token.
+
+Set :attr:`.App.fromfile_prefix_chars` to enable the feature.
+Any CLI token starting with one of these characters is treated as a file path whose contents are expanded **in-place**:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   from cyclopts import App
+
+   app = App(fromfile_prefix_chars="@")
+
+   @app.command
+   def run(host: str, port: int, description: str = ""):
+       print(host, port, description)
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+   # run.args
+   run
+   --host
+   db.example.internal
+   --port
+   5432
+   --description
+   nightly integration run
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+   $ my-app @run.args
+   db.example.internal 5432 nightly integration run
+
+The expanded arguments are ordinary CLI tokens; they go through the same parsing, conversion, validation, and command dispatch as tokens typed directly on the command line.
+This mirrors :class:`argparse.ArgumentParser`'s ``fromfile_prefix_chars``.
+
+----------------
+File Format
+----------------
+Each line of the file is a single argument; a line is **not** split on whitespace.
+Blank (and whitespace-only) lines are skipped.
+Argument files may reference other argument files:
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+   # run.args
+   run
+   @connection.args
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+   # connection.args
+   --host
+   db.example.internal
+   --port
+   5432
+
+A file that (directly or indirectly) references itself raises an error, as does a reference to a file that cannot be read.
+
+--------------------------
+Customizing the Conversion
+--------------------------
+Some argument files are nicer to write with multiple arguments per line, or with comments.
+Provide :attr:`.App.convert_arg_line_to_args` to convert each non-blank line into any number of tokens:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   import shlex
+
+   from cyclopts import App
+
+   def convert_arg_line_to_args(line: str) -> list[str]:
+       if line.startswith("#"):
+           return []
+       return shlex.split(line)
+
+   app = App(fromfile_prefix_chars="@", convert_arg_line_to_args=convert_arg_line_to_args)
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+   # run.args
+   # Connection settings.
+   run --host db.example.internal --port 5432
+
+Like other :class:`.App` attributes, ``fromfile_prefix_chars`` and ``convert_arg_line_to_args`` are inherited by subcommands.
